A||N||24||stimpy||Who has made a footwell sub enclosure? ||||5||
Z||000000||stimpy||06-01-2000||09:21 PM||||I have seen members post pics of sub enclosures that fit in the passenger footwell. I think it is  a kickass idea and I would like to replicate it. I have some ideas on how to make it but I am very interested in feedback from those who have gone down this road before.  I am planning on going to the local pull a part armed with posterboard and duct tape. My idea is to form a pattern that conforms to the footwell space, then fill it with expanding sprayfoam. Then I would trim it flush with the footrest on the side of the footwell, hollow it out and attach foamcore board to the front to mount the speaker. One of our clients is a professional fiberglass shop that can cover the foam plug with fiberglass and even gelcoat it to match interior colors. At this point he could even make a mold and replicate it over and over. Price for glass would be +- $50. <BR>Here are my questions. What size and type of speaker would be best? Could the fibergalss work be done by a mook such as myself? Where would I procure the materials? If it were cost effective to produce a small run, is anyone interested? Thanks in advance for yer feedback.<BR>||||reg||5
Z||000001||BroCar 87||06-01-2000||10:47 PM||||Hey I would be interested if you wanted to do that. I have measured the foot area height and the biggest speaker that will fit under the plastic vent pieces would be a 10" sub. I have a 10" sub (Audio Logic 375watt) there now. Its not too pretty but works great. I only have a 100watt amp going to the sub. But when I had a 400watt amp in there, IT KICKED ASS  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> If I can get a pic, I will post it.<BR>But YEA if you wanna go with a little fiberglass box, I am sure I will go and many others would go for the "run" of this.<BR>As for the size sub and type... I would prefer the 10"  and ECLIPSE are Bad @$$. <A HREF="http://www.eclipse-web.com" TARGET=_blank>www.eclipse-web.com</A>   <BR>I think this is the site. Either way. I am getting this whole ECLPISE set-up in my car. they have everything i need for my fiero. 4x6, 4x10, 8, and 10<BR>Well I took up enough space. Thanks and keep me up to date on this. OKEY DOKEY  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><BR>BroCar 87||||reg||1
Z||000002||stimpy||06-01-2000||11:09 PM||||Hey Bro, d'ya think that a 10 would get enough air out of that box? I was kida thinking 8" as I don't think it wil have much more volume then the RSM console box. BTW Eclipse makes some wild stuff. My pops had an Eclipse head unit in a LeBaron ragtop he had. Only buttons on the face were station presets- everything else was touchscreen. Way cool.<P>Still like to hear from fiberglass experts.||||reg||1
Z||000003||phillip||06-02-2000||03:35 AM||||guess i gotta figure out how to do pics eventualy. i have a footwell sub box that holds an 8. i'm about 5'11" and can sit on the passenger side without too much feeling of foot room loss, considering that if i were on the drivers side i would have pedals taking up room. a 10' box is probaly possible but i though i could do an 8" and get better results space wise. plus car stereo and fiberglass are just hobbies for me and i didn't want to bite off too much.<P>i pulled back my carpet and taped up the area liberaly ( the side of the console and the front wall as it slopes down to become the floor). i laid glass up to the level of the consoleand all over that corner of the foot well. that pretty much made the left side, back and bottom. the top and sides are 3/4" fiberboard. so it is kind of triangle shaped. size was a compleat guess and is probaly too small for my sub (jl 8w1) but it sounds ok.<P>i'm still planning to put 8's in the doors also, and switch to 3 jl 8w0 12 ohms'. that ought to do it.<P>this louisville show is coming up. i mean to be there. not to show but some one may think it might be worth getting a picture of to post. <P>forgot to mention that if you try the taping up the area idea you need to spray it with wd-40 or something similar. you will have a hard time getting ths glass shell out if you don't.<p>[This message has been edited by phillip (edited 06-03-2000).]||||reg||1
Z||000004||stimpy||06-04-2000||09:00 PM||||Well, been busy today! I took my posterboard and duct-tape and lined the footwell, taping it in to shape. Then I picked up 2 cans of spray foam and a bondo fiberglass kit. I sprayed a layer of the foam throughout my form then trimmed it to fit flush with a craft knife. Instead of foamcore I used some plastic bathtub enclosure material we had lying around. Duct taped it to the front and sprayed more foam to seal the edge of the face. <BR>Applying fiberglas- little trickier then I thought, but still easy enough for a novice. Revelation- fiberglass cloth spread out a LOT once you start spreading the resin out on it. Use small strips.<BR>Spraying foam- messy as HELL! use disposable gloves and don't let it get on your skin or clothes. I wasted a good pair of pants today.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif"> ||||reg||1
Z||000005||1FST2M6||06-04-2000||11:03 PM|||| <A HREF="http://www.fiero.nl/in-n-out.jpg" TARGET=_blank>www.fiero.nl/in-n-out.jpg</A>    I'm 6'2" and fit int the car JUST fine... 10" Solobaric with Xtant 1001dx behind the pass. seat. ||||reg||1
Z||000006||1FST2M6||06-04-2000||11:03 PM|||| <A HREF="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/in-n-out.jpg" TARGET=_blank>www.fiero.nl/uploads/in-n-out.jpg</A>    I'm 6'2" and fit int the car JUST fine... 10" Solobaric with Xtant 1001dx behind the pass. seat. ||||reg||1
Z||000007||stimpy||06-04-2000||11:12 PM||||Ahh Fast2M6, THAT"S what I'm talkin about! Please dont tell me that this enclosure is readily available. How did you make yours?  I stayed away from MDF cuz I'm a lousy carpenter and did not want to worry about airleaks. Does your box fit flush with the footrest or does it come out? I'm not at all concerned about the legroom in mine, as even at 6'6" I can fit in y car wihout having to mash my feet down into the footwell. Am a little concerned about the speaker getting kicked though, but a sturdy grill should take care of that.||||reg||1
Z||000008||Monkeyman||06-05-2000||10:39 AM||||phillip--Are you planning to put 8" subs in the doors?  The doors of what?  I can pretty much assure you that they won't fit in the doors of a Fiero.  Definitely not flush unless you don't ever plan on rolling your windows down.  It would be tough enough to put 6 1/2" speakers there without a spacer.||||reg||1
Z||000009||stimpy||06-06-2000||12:00 AM||||If ya are thinking about 8" woofer, better buy quick. According to all the stereo shops I called today, 8" woofers are going the way of the goony-bird. Looks like 10" woofer it is. Apparently, woofer technology is such that a 10" will work efficiently in as little as .5 cu ft. Problem is the cheapest 10" that I've found in todays search was $150!!! Yikes! But the search continues.||||reg||1
Z||000010||phillip||06-06-2000||09:35 AM||||i believe i can. i've done it in my s-10 blazer. they will not be flush but i think i can do it with out it looking really bulky and added on, or not too much anyway. they would be wood and fiberglass too. <P>i may do it twice. if i get to a point where i don't care about originality and i get past some other obstacles i may put some in the indy too, except i would want illusion audios ( they're a little over 2" deep) but that's all dream mode though.<P>but you dream into action.  ||||reg||1
Z||000011||dragnlo||06-06-2000||09:36 AM||||If you are wanting to mount 8" in your door and try to keep them flush, you best bet would be illusion audio. They have a mounting depth of 2.2". This is as shallow as I have found. I am wiating on the release of the new lucent series, but I have used the carbon series 8" in the kick panels of a prelude and they rock.<BR> <A HREF="http://www.illusionaudio.com/illusion/Homex.html" TARGET=_blank>http://www.illusionaudio.com/illusion/Homex.html</A>  <P><BR>Hope this helps||||reg||1
Z||000012||phillip||06-06-2000||09:46 AM||||two minds with but a single thought. yep the illusions seem like a good idea, but i'd stay with jl for my '87 since i mean to use the foot well sub with the door subs, and i dont know anyone else who makes 12 ohm subs. plus the w-o series are pretty cheap. since i'd only be planing on two in the indy ( or actually 4 since i will be using 2 8" co-axials too) i could take advantage of the illusions (if i can afford them, yeesh!).||||reg||1
Z||000013||stimpy||06-06-2000||11:03 PM||||Status report...<BR>Well,Sunday's fiberglass has pretty well cured. Today I got busy and ripped out as much of the foam as possible. Whooowee! what a mess! Ihad to use a wire grinding wheel to get it broken up into pieces I could take out, resulting in a fine coat of foamdust all over. I itch like crazy!<P>Also got my woofer. Decided on a Polk Audio dX series 10" designed for small enclosures. Sounded excellent at circuit city. especially compared to the Rockford Fosgates that were on sale. <P>Well thats it for today, more updates to follow.||||reg||1
Z||000014||BroCar 87||06-06-2000||11:25 PM||||SWWEEEEEEEEET!  Keep em coming Stimpy  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000015||Homicidal||06-07-2000||01:00 AM||||Stimpy:<P>I also would have reccomended a Polk Audio db series.  I got one of those.<P>They are made just FOR small enclosures.  Awesome speaker, but has around a $200 msrp rating.<P>I got it for free from a friend.  Check it here:<P>[url]http://www.polkaudio.com/subapril.htm[/url||||reg||1
Z||000016||Homicidal||06-07-2000||01:00 AM||||Stimpy:<P>I also would have reccomended a Polk Audio db series.  I got one of those.<P>They are made just FOR small enclosures.  Awesome speaker, but has around a $200 msrp rating.<P>I got it for free from a friend.  Check it here:<P> <A HREF="http://www.polkaudio.com/subapril.htm" TARGET=_blank>http://www.polkaudio.com/subapril.htm</A> ||||reg||1
Z||000017||1FST2M6||06-07-2000||01:04 PM||||sorry for not checking this... My box is 18mm birch plywood face with fiberglas for the rest of the enclouser covered with Matte Black Mica... it's about .38 cuft of air.. with 1.5lbs of poly fill and my Solobaric. I have great extension... from 11hz to 80hz... the Xtant helps a lot. I siezed a sub and my girlfriend thought "well since it's stuck just kick it and it'll be ok..." thats the ONLY time the sub gets kicked... oh.. Kicker replaced the sub free of charge. I now have a Kicker L7 and have to build a NEW box... Square peg won't fit in a round hole... 10" MSRP$369 I paid $249 thats what they sell for around here... no special deal. I had a PPI Pro 10 in the same enclouser and it sounded fine but the speaker itself tiped the scales at 30lbs and i wasn't willing to live with that much weight in the car... Polk makes great sub bass drivers but they require a lot of power to drive with any decent volume in such a small enclouser as the foot well of our cars. I've tried a Bostwick.. THATS CRAP! I had a JL 10w3 DVC 2ohm that was ok but for the same price the Kicker has sounded the best with the highest SPL and greatest Q.  Just what I've found...  Best of luck... what kind of amp are you using? Make sure you have a good ground and ample wire to sustain a load like a sub.. my 2ga would heat up untill i put the 2 caps on it... somthing else to think about. <p>[This message has been edited by 1FST2M6 (edited 06-07-2000).]||||reg||1
Z||000018||stimpy||06-08-2000||07:10 AM||||FST, currently I have a Phase Linear 200w amp. I eventually will go for more power, but this should do me for now. I need to see how much sound this puts down before I invest another $300-400 in a bigger amp.<P>Homicidal, thanks for the testimonial. I was curious about the difference between db and dX models, so I went to the FAQ at the link you posted. Pretty much the same speaker, dX 1just being an updated model using higher quality materials (according to Polk). I got mine for $181 out the door with cicuit city's 3 year unconditional warranty tacked on. The footwell being a vulnerable place, figured it's good insurance.||||reg||1
Z||000019||stimpy||06-11-2000||10:29 PM||||Well, it's all done and in the car!!!<BR>Yeah! I followed 2FST's lead and used plywood for the face. I also went down to the local pull-a-part and got a piece of Fiero carpeting that matches my interior and fastened it to the front and wrapped it around the side, so it looks pretty freakin close to factory. I don't have the grill yet, but I plan on spraygluing fabric to it to make it more uniform looking. <P>People, you can DO this!!!<P>I spent about $20 on materials. and maybe 2 hours total in labor, plus drying time.  I can't wait to get my amp hooked up and start annoyin the neighbors.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"> ||||reg||1
Z||000020||BroCar 87||06-11-2000||10:39 PM||||WAY TO GO STIMPY!!!   pics pics pics... lol||||reg||1
Z||000021||stimpy||06-11-2000||10:54 PM||||Soon Grasshopper.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000022||stimpy||06-12-2000||11:52 PM||||Wooohoooo! The amp is hooked up and everything works GREAT! Mrs Stimpy will have to get used to riding around with less-than-limosine footroom, but all in all it is still comfortable over in the right hand seat. I actually had to turn the gain down on the amp so as not to overpower the sound with bass, but it works very well. Probably get a 4 channel amp to run the rest of the stuff. <P>Homicidal- if you are still checking in on this thread, I HIGHLY encourage you to go this route instead of the front compartment. No drilling orcutting- totally reversible. Helps save the resale value of yer ride. And I gotta think it would sound a whole lot clearer, not to mention less advertising to thieves.<P>BroCar, will post pics asap, but due to being webtv, prob will be a while. Basically just look at FST2M6's install and picture it with tan carpeting instead of black and add a waffle grill- that's what it looks like.||||reg||1
Z||000023||BroCar 87||06-13-2000||02:14 PM||||Hey Stimpy... So when is this SMALL RUN going to start??? lol    anxiously waiting  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>BroCar 87||||reg||1
Z||000024||stimpy||06-13-2000||07:30 PM||||Hehehe. Well I do have enough cloth let to do a couple of these, but it's so freakin easy to do it would be criminal for me to try to sell these. I may see if people in my club are interested in building some, but you can do this, mon frere! BTW, what do you have your speaker in presently? ||||reg||1
